<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks intervention exports.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks intervention exports.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders bid for the export of 87,500 tonnes of intervention rye and 64,000 tonnes of intervention barley to third countries at a weekly European tender, intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In addition, BLE received bids for the export of 14,500 tonnes of wheat from intervention as aid under the World Food Programme.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
